# Managed by make secrets-pull-aws.
# Variables for Storybook, generated from AWS Secrets Manager by `make secrets-pull-aws`
# (docs/project_plan.md section 7). Edit the secret, not this file: the next pull overwrites it.
# `make setup` copies this sample to .env.local, which is not committed.
#
# Storybook (Vite builder) exposes only variables prefixed with STORYBOOK_ to stories, as
# import.meta.env.STORYBOOK_*. They are embedded in the built Storybook and readable by anyone
# who can open it, so never put real secrets (private API keys) in them.
# Values may contain any character except a carriage return; a few combinations of quotes and
# backslashes (e.g. a value ending in a backslash) are rejected because .env cannot hold them.

# Example: base URL of an API that stories call. Not used by the sample components.
STORYBOOK_EXAMPLE_API_URL=
